            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_d31e04d6">C4:010</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_id3a40c9a5" xml:lang="de">Die natürliche Historie des Eider-Vogels</title>
            <title type="original" xml:id="title_979611fa" xml:lang="da">Eder-Fuglens Beskrivelse </title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_897dccdc">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_id2b5a9d3b">Morten Thrane Brünniche</persName>
               <persName role="translator" xml:id="persName_b5c20d68">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_3917da5b">Adam Gottlob Moltke</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_9a4673a2">Otto Thott</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_idbe0f39e5">
               <date isodate="1763" xml:id="date_c9daf16d">1763</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_idb393d313">
               <p xml:id="idm81">In 1763 the twenty-six-year old zoologist, <persName xml:id="idm82" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Morten Thrane Brünniche</persName>, published his study on the common eider. A German translation by Scheibe appeared later that same year. The book was reviewed in several journals among others <rend xml:id="idm83" fontstyle="italic">Göttingische Anzeigen</rend> and <rend xml:id="idm84" fontstyle="italic">Gazette litteraire de l'Europe</rend>.The name of the translator does not appear on the title page but according to Ehrencron-Müller, <rend xml:id="idm85" fontstyle="italic">Bibliotheca Danica</rend>, it is Scheibe.</p>
            </history>
